   "chapter": 6,
   "data": {
    "t": "h2",
    "text": "The calling ḥarf يَا"
   },
   "html": "<h2><span class=\"num\">6</span>The calling ḥarf يَا</h2>"
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "t": "p",
   "chapter": 6,
   "data": {
    "t": "p",
    "text": "Use {يَا} to call someone. After {يَا} a name, or a single noun for the person you call, takes one damma. It never takes tanween. This damma is fixed. The called word is in the place of naṣb ({فِي مَحَلِّ نَصْبٍ})."
   },
   "html": "<p class=\"s0p\">Use <bdi class=\"ab\">يَا</bdi> to call someone. After <bdi class=\"ab\">يَا</bdi> a name, or a single noun for the person you call, takes one damma. It never takes tanween. This damma is fixed. The called word is in the place of naṣb (<bdi class=\"ab\">فِي مَحَلِّ نَصْبٍ</bdi>).</p>"
  },
